WEBVTT

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:10.840
-What is it?
-Can you see it?

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:14.520
-What the heck is up there?
-Woody, who's up there with ya?

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:17.800
-(COUGHING)
-SLINKY: Woody?

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:21.000
-What are you doing under the bed?
-Uh, nothin'. Uh, nothin'.

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:23.720
I'm sure Andy was just
a little excited, that's all.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:26.560
Too much cake and ice cream,
I suppose. It's just a mistake!

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:30.400
Well, that mistake is sitting
in your spot, Woody. (CHUCKLES)

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:33.680
-(GASPS) Have you been replaced?
-What did I tell you earlier?

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.600
No one is getting replaced.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:39.400
Now, let's all be polite and give
whatever it is up there

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:43.200
a nice, big
Andy's-room welcome.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:01.320
(GULPS)

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:06.040
(HEAVY BREATHING)

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:09.920
-(BUZZES)
-Buzz Lightyear to Star Command.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:11.920
Come in, Star Command.

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:13.720
-(BUZZES)
-Star Command, come in.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:14.840
Do you read me?

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:18.240
Why don't they answer?
(GASPS) My ship!

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:24.280
Blast! This'll take weeks to repair.

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:27.960
Buzz Lightyear mission log,
stardate 4-0-7-2.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:31.320
My ship has run off course
en route to sector 12.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.880
I've crash-landed
on a strange planet.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:36.440
The impact must've awoken me
from hypersleep.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:41.320
Terrain seems a bit unstable.

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:44.480
No readout yet
if the air is breathable.

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:47.640
And there seems to be no sign
of intelligent life anywhere.

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:49.040
-Hello!
-(KARATE YELL)

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:52.080
(SCREAMS) Whoa! H-Hey!
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:54.480
-Did I frighten you? Didn't mean to.
-(BUZZING)

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:56.960
-Sorry. Howdy. My name is Woody.
-(BUZZING CONTINUES)

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:00.920
And this is Andy's room.
That's all I wanted to say.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:03.720
And also, there has been
a bit of a mix-up.

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:06.040
This is my spot, see,
the bed here.

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:08.600
Local law enforcement.
It's about time you got here.

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:11.600
I'm Buzz Lightyear, Space Ranger,
Universe Protection Unit.

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:13.920
My ship has crash-landed here
by mistake.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.840
Yes, it is a mistake because,
you see, the bed here is my spot.

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:19.480
I need to repair
my turbo boosters.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:22.680
Do you people still use fossil fuel, or
have you discovered crystallic fusion?

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:25.160
-Well, let's see. We got double-A's.
-(GASPS)

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:27.160
Watch yourself!
Halt! Who goes there?

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:29.640
Don't shoot!
It's okay. Friends.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:33.480
-Do you know these life-forms?
-Yes! They're Andy's toys.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:35.880
All right, everyone,
you're clear to come up.

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:38.600
I am Buzz Lightyear.
I come in peace.

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:42.360
Oh, I'm so glad
you're not a dinosaur!

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:44.400
Wh-why, thank you!

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:47.200
Now, thank you all
for your kind welcome!

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:50.040
-Say, what's that button do?
-I'll show you.

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:52.200
VOICE BOX:
Buzz Lightyear to the rescue!

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:53.240
TOYS: Oh!

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:55.920
Hey, Woody's got something like that.
His is a pull string.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.200
-Only it's...
-Only it sounds like a car ran over it.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:02.040
HAMM: Oh, yeah, but not like this.
This is a quality sound system.

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:03.680
Probably all copper wiring, huh?

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:07.000
So, uh, where you from?
Singapore? Hong Kong?

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:09.360
Well, no. Actually, I-I'm stationed up
in the Gamma Quadrant of Sector Four.

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:14.320
As a member of the elite
Universe Protection Unit

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:15.800
of the Space Ranger Corps,

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:18.560
I protect the galaxy
from the threat of invasion

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:22.760
from the evil Emperor Zurg,
sworn enemy of the Galactic Alliance.

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:25.480
Oh, really?
I'm from Playskool.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:27.840
And I'm from Mattel.
Well, I'm not really from Mattel.

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:31.680
I'm actually from a smaller company that
was purchased in a leveraged buyout.

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:33.600
You'd think they'd never seen
a new toy before.

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.400
Well, sure. Look at him.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:38.240
He's got more gadgets on him
than a Swiss Army knife.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:41.080
-(BUZZING)
-Ah, ah, ah, ah! Please be careful.

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.640
You don't want to be in the way
when my laser goes off.

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:46.240
Hey, a laser! How come
you don't have a laser, Woody?

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:49.280
It's not a laser! It's a...
It's a little light bulb that blinks.

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:51.080
-What's with him?
-Laser envy.

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:52.400
All right, that's enough!

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:55.840
Look, we're all very impressed
with Andy's new toy.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:58.320
-Toy?
-T-O-Y. Toy!

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:02.400
Excuse me, I think the word
you're searching for is "Space Ranger."

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:06.920
The word I'm searching for I can't say
because there's preschool toys present.

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:08.520
Gettin' kinda tense, aren't ya?

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:11.640
Uh, Mr. Lightyear,
uh, now, I'm curious.

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:14.360
What does a Space Ranger
actually do?

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:16.480
He's not a Space Ranger!

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:20.200
He doesn't fight evil
or, or shoot lasers or fly!

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:21.680
Excuse me.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:26.280
-TOYS: Ooh!
-Oh, impressive wingspan! Very good!

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:31.120
Oh, what? What?
These are plastic. He can't fly!

00:04:31.160 --> 00:04:34.640
They are a terillium-carbonic alloy,
and I can fly.

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:38.000
-No, you can't.
-(SIGHS) Yes, I can.

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:39.120
-You can't.
-Can.

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:40.920
Can't. Can't. Can't!

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:43.440
I tell you, I could fly around
this room with my eyes closed!

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:47.680
-Okay, then, Mr. Light Beer, prove it.
-All right, then, I will.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:49.680
Stand back, everyone!

00:04:53.320 --> 00:04:55.320
(ELECTRONIC HUM)

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:00.160
To infinity and beyond!

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:14.160
(AIRPLANE WHIRRING)

